# TypeScript

Use strict types. Prefer `unknown` plus narrowing over `any`. Export explicit types for public component props and API payloads.

Handle promise failures at the boundary that can show or log them. Do not leave floating promises in UI event handlers.

Keep server data, URL state, and ephemeral UI state distinct. Do not duplicate a server cache in ad-hoc globals.

Validate external input at the edge. Types do not replace runtime validation for network, tool, or user payload data.

Match existing module style. Do not introduce a second state or data-fetching library without a stated gap.
